  "key_findings": [
    "ARM H FAILS G4 AT EVERY SIZE. The local Hamiltonian density's connected two-point function scales as chord^-8.5, -7.7, -7.2 at n = 16, 20, 24 (gate: 4 within 0.3). Its excitation is dominated by lattice-scale modes (at n = 10, 27% of its weight lies above the 40 lowest eigenstates; the largest weights sit at |s| = 3..5). The asymptotic Delta = 2 regime is not reached on rings this size.",
    "ARM H IS NEVERTHELESS THE RIGHT OPERATOR IN THE IR: G5 passes at n = 16, 20, 24. <eps|O_H(k=0)|GS> vanishes to 1e-13 relative to <T|O_H(k=2)|GS> (the Kramers-Wannier structural zero), and the |T> state is found by sector-projected Lanczos at Delta_T/Delta_eps = 1.981, 1.988, 1.991.",
    "THE FORCE IS IDENTICALLY ZERO FOR ARM E AT h = 1: F(dr) = 0 to 1e-14 for every separation at n = 12, 16, 20, 24. At h = 0.9 and h = 2 it is nonzero. Scanning O = op_T + c op_X at n = 12, F scales as (1 - c)^2 approaching c = 1: the energy-difference observable responds ONLY to the KW-even admixture of the probe. The single-site KW-odd energy density is invisible to it.",
    "CONSEQUENCE FOR SIM-2026-074: the ring 'energy-density exponent' 1.83 measured with Z_jZ_{j+1} alone is a cross term between that operator's KW-even and KW-odd parts, not the eps two-point exponent. The v5 Zenodo notice was reworded on 2026-09-06 to remove the channel attribution.",
    "THE RETRY (Gaussian-smeared probes, sigma = 1.5 sites, |m| <= 4, width fixed 2026-09-07 before any smeared result existed) ALSO FAILS G4: smeared H two-point exponent 2.57 / 4.97 / 6.57 at n = 16/20/24 with local slopes running from -1 to +30 across the window (no power law). Smearing makes Arm E's force NONZERO (exponent ~8.2-8.6, exponential-like) and moves its two-point exponent to ~4.1-4.3; both effects are recorded, not interpreted.",
    "E-ARM G5 FAILS BY DESIGN, NOT PHYSICS: <T|O_E(k=2)|GS> / <eps|O_E(k=0)|GS> = 1.4e-2, 8.7e-3, 6.1e-3 at n = 16/20/24, shrinking ~1/n. The lattice KW map carries a half-site shift, so only k = 0 modes have exact KW parity; the k = 2 structural zero registered for Arm E was mis-specified. Arm E is void anyway (F = 0, no plateau).",
    "CONTROLS: G1 to 1e-15 at every size; h = 2 control CONTROL_CLEAN at every size and in the retry."
  ],
  "counterfactual_novelty_note": "Outcome space registered: N / DEV / C / D / VOID. VOID via G4 was a live possibility named in advance. The structural zero F[O_E] = 0 was NOT anticipated and is the one genuinely new fact; it is a property of the observable, not of the CFT, and is recorded at Level 2 (method).",
  "what_would_change_this": "A probe whose own two-point function reaches the Delta = 2 regime inside the fit window: either much larger n (free-fermion machinery could reach hundreds of sites for the two-point function but the energy-difference force needs the interacting-state machinery) or a different observable. Neither is inside the pre-registered scope.",
